# Ignore list for Eagle, a PCB layout tool

# Backup files
*.s#?
*.b#?
*.l#?

# Eagle project file
# It contains a serial number and references to the file structure
# on your computer.
# comment the following line if you want to have your project file included.
eagle.epf

# CAM files
*.$$$
*.cmp
*.ly2
*.l15
*.sol
*.plc
*.stc
*.sts
*.crc
*.crs

*.dri
*.drl
*.gpi
*.pls

*.drd
*.drd.*

*.info

*.eps


# PlatformIO
.pio/

# Oven-specific and personal: run captures, measured behaviour, handover notes.
# Kept on disk, deliberately never tracked -- purged from history 2026-09-04.
logs/
REWORK_NOTES.md
HARDWARE_CHECKS.md
PORTING_ANALYSIS.md

# NO SCREENSHOTS, EVER.
#
# One of the oven page carries the LAN address in the browser address bar --
# the same class of thing the 2026-09-04 history purge removed -- and a run
# trace is oven-specific information that does not leave this machine.
#
# Screenshot tools drop their output in the repo root, so the root is closed to
# images entirely rather than trying to guess every naming convention. This
# does NOT disturb the images already tracked: .gitignore has no effect on a
# tracked file, so images/ and the existing root photos stay exactly as they
# are. If a genuinely wanted image ever needs to live in the root, "git add -f"
# is the deliberate override.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.gif
/*.webp
/*.bmp

# ...and by name, wherever they land.
Screenshot*
screenshot*
Screen Shot*
*screen_shot*
